The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/equipment-der/equip-der-06-pv-inverter-priority-reactive-power.md`.

**Summary of findings (5 total, 2 Medium / 3 Low):**

| # | Severity | Issue |
|---|----------|-------|
| 1 | Medium | `ReactiveSetpoint { kvar: 0.0 }` is indistinguishable from "no Q setpoint," causing static PF to override the explicit zero command |
| 2 | Medium | PF enforcement applied as post-processing clip rather than integrated constraint (matches OCHRE behavior) |
| 3 | Low | PF-derived Q computed from pre-inverter-clip P — logically suboptimal though not incorrect |
| 4 | Low | Var-priority Q sign derived from stored `q_setpoint_kvar` field rather than function parameter |
| 5 | Low | `enforce_min_pf` forces Q=0 at P=0 (matches OCHRE; may surprise controllers expecting nighttime reactive support) |

The priority modes (Watt/Var/CPF) are implemented correctly and produce the same constraint resolution as OCHRE. The `sqrt(P²+Q²)` enforcement against inverter kVA rating and DC-to-AC ratio clipping are both handled inside `apply_inverter_limits` at `mod.rs:269–320`. The main actionable issue is Finding 1 — the need to distinguish an explicit zero-var command from an absent Q setpoint.
